<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29641" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύσχρηστ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χράομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hard to use, inconvenient</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔχρηστος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Aph.</u>
				2.54
			</span></i>, cf. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				221 vii 14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππικὸν στράτευμα ἐν νυκτὶ . . δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					3.3.26
				</span></i>
			; <i>intractable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύνες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					3.11
				</span></i>
			; of troops, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				4.11.8
			</span></i> (
				Sup.
			); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἐξουσία</span>
			<i>hard to use well</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				8.103
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύσχρηστα</span>
			<i>inconveniences</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				7.5.3
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				4.8
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τως</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, διακεῖσθαι</span> to be <i>in difficulties,
				unmanageable</i>, of ships, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				1.61.4
			</span></i>; of troops, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαλλάττειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					4.64.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Aem.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			:—synon. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ
			χρησίμως</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				17.2.4
			</span></i>.</div>
